### What is Apache Spark and why does it need Databricks?

Apache Spark is the open-source distributed compute engine, but using it in production means provisioning machines, installing Spark, configuring the cluster manager, tuning memory, setting up storage, managing libraries, securing it, and monitoring it. Databricks was founded by the same people who created Spark to deliver all of that as a managed cloud service.

```python
# Same PySpark code runs on vanilla Spark or Databricks
df = spark.read.parquet(
    "s3://national-bank-lake/raw/txns/")
result = df.groupBy("account_id").sum("amount")
result.show(5)
```

```text
+----------+-----------+
|account_id|sum(amount)|
+----------+-----------+
|   SAV2001|  450000.00|
|   CUR3002| 1250000.00|
|   SAV2005|  320000.00|
+----------+-----------+
# Same code, but Databricks Runtime runs it faster
```

### What is the Databricks Runtime?

The Databricks Runtime is a performance-tuned distribution of Spark with extra optimizations such as the Photon vectorized engine, caching improvements, and tuned defaults. The same code often runs considerably faster than on vanilla Spark without any changes.

```java
package com.bank.platform;

public class DatabricksRuntime {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Databricks Runtime optimizations:");
        System.out.println("  1. Photon: vectorized C++ engine");
        System.out.println("  2. Adaptive query execution tuned");
        System.out.println("  3. Caching improvements");
        System.out.println("  4. Optimized shuffle service");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Same PySpark/Scala/SQL code,"
            + " faster execution.");
    }
}
```

```text
Databricks Runtime optimizations:
  1. Photon: vectorized C++ engine
  2. Adaptive query execution tuned
  3. Caching improvements
  4. Optimized shuffle service

Same PySpark/Scala/SQL code, faster execution.
```

### What is Delta Lake and why is it the default?

Delta Lake, created by Databricks and open-sourced, is the default storage layer. It brings ACID transactions, schema enforcement, time travel, and efficient upserts on top of Parquet files in cloud object storage, turning a raw data lake into a reliable lakehouse.

```python
# Delta Lake: ACID on the lake
df.write.format("delta").mode("append").save(
    "s3://national-bank-lake/curated/txns_delta")

# Time travel: read yesterday's version
spark.read.format("delta") \
    .option("timestampAsOf", "2024-10-28") \
    .load("s3://national-bank-lake/curated/txns_delta") \
    .show(3)

# MERGE: upsert atomically
from delta.tables import DeltaTable
delta_table = DeltaTable.forPath(spark,
    "s3://national-bank-lake/curated/txns_delta")
delta_table.alias("t").merge(
    updates.alias("u"), "t.txn_id = u.txn_id"
).whenMatchedUpdateAll() \
 .whenNotMatchedInsertAll() \
 .execute()
```

### What is Unity Catalog?

Unity Catalog provides centralized governance: one place to manage access control, auditing, data lineage, and discovery across workspaces. This matters enormously in a regulated industry like banking.

```sql
-- Unity Catalog: fine-grained access control
GRANT SELECT ON TABLE curated.transactions
TO `analysts@nationalbank.in`;

-- Column-level masking for PII
ALTER TABLE curated.transactions
ALTER COLUMN pan_number
SET MASK mask_pan;

-- Data lineage: trace where data came from
-- Unity Catalog automatically tracks which tables
-- feed into which downstream tables
```

```java
package com.bank.platform;

public class UnityCatalogBenefits {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Unity Catalog provides:");
        System.out.println("  1. Access control (table, column level)");
        System.out.println("  2. Audit logging (who read what, when)");
        System.out.println("  3. Data lineage (source -> target)");
        System.out.println("  4. Discovery (search across all data)");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Critical for banking regulation.");
    }
}
```

```text
Unity Catalog provides:
  1. Access control (table, column level)
  2. Audit logging (who read what, when)
  3. Data lineage (source -> target)
  4. Discovery (search across all data)

Critical for banking regulation.
```

### How does cluster management work?

Cluster management is automated with autoscaling, auto-termination of idle clusters, and different cluster types for interactive versus production work. This controls cost and reduces operational burden.

```json
{
  "cluster_name": "bank-etl-prod",
  "spark_version": "14.3.x-scala2.12",
  "autoscale": {
    "min_workers": 2,
    "max_workers": 20
  },
  "autotermination_minutes": 30,
  "node_type_id": "i3.xlarge",
  "driver_node_type_id": "i3.xlarge"
}
```

```java
package com.bank.platform;

public class ClusterManagement {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Cluster types:");
        System.out.println("  Interactive: notebooks, ad-hoc analysis");
        System.out.println("  Job: scheduled ETL, auto-terminate after");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Cost controls:");
        System.out.println("  Autoscale: 2 to 20 workers based on load");
        System.out.println("  Auto-terminate: shut down after 30 min idle");
        System.out.println("  Spot instances: 60-90% cheaper for fault-tolerant jobs");
    }
}
```

```text
Cluster types:
  Interactive: notebooks, ad-hoc analysis
  Job: scheduled ETL, auto-terminate after

Cost controls:
  Autoscale: 2 to 20 workers based on load
  Auto-terminate: shut down after 30 min idle
  Spot instances: 60-90% cheaper for fault-tolerant jobs
```

### What is the lakehouse thesis?

The lakehouse thesis is that you no longer need a separate data lake and warehouse. Delta Lake plus Spark plus SQL endpoints give you cheap storage and warehouse-style performance and reliability in one place.

```python
# SQL endpoint: warehouse-like experience on Delta Lake
# Analysts query with plain SQL, no Spark knowledge needed
# SELECT * FROM curated.daily_summary
# WHERE branch = 'Mumbai Central'
# AND   month  = '2024-10'

# Under the hood: Photon engine on Delta Parquet files
# Same data, lake storage cost, warehouse query speed
```

```java
package com.bank.platform;

public class LakehouseThesis {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Before lakehouse:");
        System.out.println("  Lake (raw) -> ETL -> Warehouse (clean)");
        System.out.println("  Two systems, data copied between them.");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("With lakehouse:");
        System.out.println("  Lake storage + Delta log = one system");
        System.out.println("  ETL, analytics, ML on same data.");
        System.out.println("  No copying between lake and warehouse.");
    }
}
```

```text
Before lakehouse:
  Lake (raw) -> ETL -> Warehouse (clean)
  Two systems, data copied between them.

With lakehouse:
  Lake storage + Delta log = one system
  ETL, analytics, ML on same data.
  No copying between lake and warehouse.
```

### What are the trade-offs of adopting Databricks?

Databricks is not a fork of Spark that locks you in at the code level. Your Spark code is portable and Delta Lake is open source. However, features like Photon, Unity Catalog, Delta Live Tables, and managed services are Databricks-specific value you give up if you move off the platform.

```java
package com.bank.platform;

public class DatabricksTradeoffs {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Portable (open source):");
        System.out.println("  - PySpark / Scala / SQL code");
        System.out.println("  - Delta Lake format and protocol");
        System.out.println("  - MLflow experiment tracking");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Databricks-specific (not portable):");
        System.out.println("  - Photon engine");
        System.out.println("  - Unity Catalog");
        System.out.println("  - Delta Live Tables");
        System.out.println("  - Managed clusters and notebooks");
        System.out.println();
        System.out.println("Trade: cost + some lock-in for"
            + " less ops + faster execution + governance.");
    }
}
```

```text
Portable (open source):
  - PySpark / Scala / SQL code
  - Delta Lake format and protocol
  - MLflow experiment tracking

Databricks-specific (not portable):
  - Photon engine
  - Unity Catalog
  - Delta Live Tables
  - Managed clusters and notebooks

Trade: cost + some lock-in for less ops + faster execution + governance.
```

